            },
            {
              "id": "note",
              "kind": "note",
              "col": -0.35,
              "row": 5.15,
              "width": 400,
              "label": "Assumptions\n\n1. Delivery is at-least-once end to end, so every transform is idempotent and keyed on event id.\n\n2. No synchronous service-to-service calls: components meet only at the stream, the bus or the queue, and each scales on its own backlog.\n\n3. All compute is serverless or auto-scaled. Nothing on the critical path is a single instance.\n\n4. Every queue has a DLQ (5 receives), every job a Step Functions catch, every write a retry with jitter.\n\n5. eu-west-1 across 3 AZs; RPO 15 min / RTO 1 h via S3 cross-region replication and Redshift snapshots to us-east-1.\n\n6. AWS Config, Secrets Manager and AWS Backup are enabled account-wide and left off the canvas."
            }
          ],
